{"default":"<p>Mr. Mehul&nbsp;Grover is an officer of the Indian Audit and Accounts Service (IA&amp;AS), belonging to the 2014 batch, currently serving as Director at the Office of the Principal Director of Audit, Washington. He holds a Bachelor of Technology in Electronics and Communication and has further strengthened his academic profile with a Post Graduate Diploma in Environmental Law. He is also presently pursuing a Post Graduate Diploma in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning.</p>

<p>He brings with him diverse professional experience across Local Bodies, Revenue, Forest, and Defence Audit. Prior to his current assignment, he served as Director (Training and Research) at the International Centre for Environmental Audit and Sustainable Development (iCED), where he managed national and international training programmes in Environmental and Extractive Industries Audit. He has also participated in international engagements, including training at UCLA, Los Angeles, the ASOSAI Seminar on Environmental Auditing, and audit-related assignments with international organizations such as the ILO in Italy and Switzerland. He is a recipient of the CAG&rsquo;s Award for Public Sector Auditing for his work on the performance audit of degradation of the Kshipra River. His interests include continuous learning in areas such as environmental governance and emerging technologies, as well as meditation.</p>","hi":"<p>Mr. Mehul&nbsp;Grover is an officer of the Indian Audit and Accounts Service (IA&amp;AS), belonging to the 2014 batch, currently serving as Director at the Office of the Principal Director of Audit, Washington. He holds a Bachelor of Technology in Electronics and Communication and has further strengthened his academic profile with a Post Graduate Diploma in Environmental Law. He is also presently pursuing a Post Graduate Diploma in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning.</p>

<p>He brings with him diverse professional experience across Local Bodies, Revenue, Forest, and Defence Audit. Prior to his current assignment, he served as Director (Training and Research) at the International Centre for Environmental Audit and Sustainable Development (iCED), where he managed national and international training programmes in Environmental and Extractive Industries Audit. He has also participated in international engagements, including training at UCLA, Los Angeles, the ASOSAI Seminar on Environmental Auditing, and audit-related assignments with international organizations such as the ILO in Italy and Switzerland. He is a recipient of the CAG&rsquo;s Award for Public Sector Auditing for his work on the performance audit of degradation of the Kshipra River. His interests include continuous learning in areas such as environmental governance and emerging technologies, as well as meditation.</p>"}

{"default":"<p >Dr. Sanjay Rao Kamineni is a 2016 batch officer of the Indian Audit and Accounts Service (IAAS) and currently serves as Director, Centre of Excellence for Financial Audit (CoEFA), Hyderabad.He cleared the Civil Services Examination (UPSC) in 2015 and completed his foundational training at the National Academy of Audit and Accounts, Shimla, supplemented by specialised exposure at the United Nations, New York, and participation in the Indo Kuwait Bilateral Seminar.Dr. Sanjay Kamineni also holds the charge of Senior Deputy Accountant General (AMG II), Telangana, in the Office of the Principal Accountant General (Audit), Telangana, where he oversees audits of key Economic Sector Departments such as Finance, Energy, Industries, IT, Agriculture, and Civil Supplies, as well as the Financial Audit of Statutory Corporations and Government Companies of the Government of Telangana. He earlier served as Deputy Accountant General (Audit) in Tripura (2018 to 2021).</p>

<p >Dr. Sanjay Kamineni holds an MBBS from Osmania Medical College, Hyderabad, and hails from Karimnagar, Telangana. Outside work, he enjoys travelling, running, and playing tennis.</p>","hi":"<p >डॉ. संजय राव कामिनेनी इंडियन ऑडिट एंड अकाउंट्स सर्विस (IAAS) के 2016 बैच के ऑफिसर हैं और अभी हैदराबाद में सेंटर ऑफ़ एक्सीलेंस फॉर फाइनेंशियल ऑडिट (CoEFA) के डायरेक्टर हैं।tउन्होंने 2015 में सिविल सर्विसेज़ एग्जामिनेशन (UPSC) पास किया और शिमला में नेशनल एकेडमी ऑफ़ ऑडिट एंड अकाउंट्स में अपनी बेसिक ट्रेनिंग पूरी की, जिसके साथ यूनाइटेड नेशंस, न्यूयॉर्क में स्पेशलाइज़्ड एक्सपोज़र और इंडो-कुवैत बाइलेटरल सेमिनार में हिस्सा लिया। डॉ. संजय कामिनेनी तेलंगाना के प्रिंसिपल अकाउंटेंट जनरल (ऑडिट) के ऑफिस में सीनियर डिप्टी अकाउंटेंट जनरल (AMG II), तेलंगाना का भी चार्ज संभालते हैं, जहाँ वे फाइनेंस, एनर्जी, इंडस्ट्रीज़, IT, एग्रीकल्चर और सिविल सप्लाइज़ जैसे मुख्य इकोनॉमिक सेक्टर डिपार्टमेंट्स के ऑडिट के साथ-साथ तेलंगाना सरकार के स्टैच्युटरी कॉर्पोरेशन्स और सरकारी कंपनियों के फाइनेंशियल ऑडिट की देखरेख करते हैं। इससे पहले उन्होंने त्रिपुरा (2018 से 2021) में डिप्टी अकाउंटेंट जनरल (ऑडिट) के तौर पर काम किया था।</p>

<p >डॉ. संजय कामिनेनी ने हैदराबाद के उस्मानिया मेडिकल कॉलेज से MBBS की डिग्री ली है और वे करीमनगर, तेलंगाना के रहने वाले हैं। काम के अलावा, उन्हें घूमना, दौड़ना और टेनिस खेलना पसंद है।</p>"}
